---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Open Source and Technical Collaboration | MD Anik Hasan"
  description="Public repositories and an honest invitation to collaborate on practical software, native Windows work, automation, and first-principles AI learning."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Contribution board"
    title="Open to useful work, clear scope, and shared learning."
    intro="I’m open to contributing to meaningful open-source projects where I can learn the system and provide concrete work. This is separate from my paid website and software services."
    workshop="Contribution Board"
  />

  <section class="plain-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Good collaboration areas</p>
    <h2>Practical software with a real issue to solve.</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        The clearest areas for collaboration are native Windows work, Python automation, practical
        software tools, and learning language-model systems from first principles.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not claim a large external contribution history or maintainer status. I would rather
        begin with a well-scoped issue, understand the repository’s conventions, and produce a
        change the maintainers can evaluate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="repository-list" aria-labelledby="repository-title">
    <h2 id="repository-title">Verified public repositories</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/mdanikhasan-dev/Soctukit">SoctuKit</a></h3>
        <p>
          Public release repository for the built native Windows product. Source is not included.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/mdanikhasan-dev/UIU-Discord_Bot">UIU Discord Bot</a></h3>
        <p>
          Python and Discord automation for UIU notices, calendar information, and server utilities.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/mdanikhasan-dev">GitHub profile</a></h3>
        <p>The verified public account for current repositories and future contribution history.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="plain-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start with context</p>
    <h2>Send the repository, issue, and expected result.</h2>
    <p>
      A useful first message explains the project, links the issue or discussion, names the language
      and environment, and describes the help you need. Use the
      <a href="/contact/">professional contact options</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
